# Claude Code per-user state (D17 hygiene + Sprint 0.1 acceptance)
# .claude/commands/ and .claude/settings.json ARE committed (repo-shared);
# .claude/settings.local.json holds per-machine permission grants — NEVER commit.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Local dev kickoff: scripts/dev.sh is tracked (portable, machine-agnostic);
# /dev.sh at repo root is gitignored as the per-machine override slot if you
# want different ports, extra setup steps, etc. without committing them.
# Note the leading slash: gitignore patterns without it match at any depth,
# which would unintentionally ignore scripts/dev.sh too.
/dev.sh
# Infra notes — real Azure values (tenant ID, subscription ID, resource names,
# App Insights connection string, deployment tokens). Per D17 + DEVELOPER_GUIDE
# "Public-repo hygiene", real Azure resource names + identifiers never land in
# committed files. The `.example` templates ARE committed; the populated
# `*-resources.md` files are NOT. Sprint 1.1+ populates these locally.
# (Path is `infra/` at repo root, per the canonical location established in
# Sprint 0.2 / DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md repo layout — NOT `docs/infra/`.)
infra/dev-resources.md
infra/prod-resources.md
